{"block":"Blocked: pkill and killall match by pattern, and pkill -f matches against full command lines, including this agent's own shell: that is how it kills the session it is running in. If the target is a process you started with the process tool, stop it there (action \"stop\") with its id. Otherwise list first and kill explicitly: pgrep -a <pattern> to see every match with its command line, check that none of them is something you did not mean, then kill <pid> for the ones you chose."}
